KG42.register("rules-354165b95a8d1565aa85d804",{"id":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R012","paper":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R012","mechanism_id":"M03","name":"Local market coordinator","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"Each customer's maximum and minimum load-variation values are approved by, or at least known to, the aggregator. Scope: Robust collaborative scheduling with bounded customer load variations. The aggregator calculates the worst-case load variation at each iteration. Scope: Distributed robust collaborative scheduling using the iterative algorithm in (24). Condition: At each iteration.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.local_operator under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Distributed robust collaborative scheduling using the iterative algorithm in (24). | Robust collaborative scheduling with bounded customer load variations.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e21"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each customer's maximum and minimum load-variation values are approved by, or at least known to, the aggregator. Scope: Robust collaborative scheduling with bounded customer load variations.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The aggregator calculates the worst-case load variation at each iteration. Scope: Distributed robust collaborative scheduling using the iterative algorithm in (24). Condition: At each iteration.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-54c42059a7-p06-c2r2__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"1224","section":"V. Uncertainty in Load Demands","anchor_text":"EV as xi,App + ei. For simplicity, we assume that when the load variation occur, each customer chang","equation_id":"(18)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We define the uncertain load variation in customer i's energy consumption for its residential appliances at time-slot t as e_i^t. Then, we can represent customer i's actual energy consumption for its residential appliances not including the EV as x_{i,App}^t + e_i^t. For simplicity, we assume that when the load variation occur, each customer change the total energy consumption by the same amount of energy as the load variation so that the total energy consumption of customer i at time-slot t is represented as x_{i,Tot}^t + e_i^t. We assume that the uncertain load variation is bounded in the following uncertainty set: \\mathcal{E} = \\{\\bar{e} \\mid e_i^{min,t} \\le e_i^t \\le e_i^{max,t}, \\ \\forall i\\in I, t\\in T\\}, \\quad (18) where e_i^{min,t} and e_i^{max,t} denote the minimum and maximum values of load variation e_i^t, respectively. The maximum and minimum values of each customer's load variation are approved by or at least known to the aggregator (e.g., through the history database)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e21","location":{"location_id":"src-54c42059a7-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M03-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":"1225","section":"V. Uncertainty in Load Demands","anchor_text":"SCHEDULING WITH ELECTRIC VEHICLES IN THE SMART GRID 1225 i∈I eti(¯x(k)), ∀t ∈T as well as the sum en","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the iterative algorithm in (24), customer i requires the information about its worst-case load variation, e_i^t(\\bar{x}^{(k)}), \\forall t\\in T, and the sum of worst-case load variation for other customers, \\sum_{i\\in I} e_i^t(\\bar{x}^{(k)}), \\forall t\\in T as well as the sum energy consumption of other customers at each iteration. The worst-case load variation \\bar{e}(\\bar{x}) is calculated by the aggregator at each iteration. Since each customer requires only the sum of worst-case load variation and the sum of energy consumption for other customers, the iterative algorithm in (24) can be conducted in a distributed manner at each customer i by updating those information through the communication network between the aggregator and customers."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No optimization or operational decision variable is declared by this rule. The source's energy-scheduling variables x_{i,App}^t and x_{i,Tot}^t are used in the clearing formulation and are not introduced by the frozen coordination statements.","empty_theta_reason":"No numeric or fixed parameter is declared in the frozen rule. The bounds e_i^{min,t} and e_i^{max,t} are mentioned as approved/known in e15, but the rule does not give a parameter domain/value or use them in an explicit expression; formalizing them would require the clearing uncertainty-set context not present in V."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-clearing","v141-a-M03-coordination","v141-a-M04-clearing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","quote":"The maximum and minimum values of each customer's load variation are approved by or at least known to the aggregator (e.g., through the history database)."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e21","quote":"The worst-case load variation \\bar{e}(\\bar{x}) is calculated by the aggregator at each iteration."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"a020a1c598ba892b6d4aa442ae8b1a55ab4287faeb58ae22ccdc69097e4c86ac","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"This rule is a procedural coordination rule: C001 records approval/known bounds and C002 records that the aggregator computes a worst-case load variation at each iteration. The frozen rule's V contains only coordination.local_operator, and its own evidence does not state an explicit formula for this operator; the source's worst-case optimization formulas (20)-(21) belong to M03 clearing and are not represented in this rule's V. Therefore no supported x/theta or formal expression is asserted. The patch remains provisional under the experiment's unreviewed B evidence policy.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C001 is a procedural approval/known-bounds requirement assigned to the local coordinator. coordination.local_operator is the sole frozen node in this rule, and E supplies no edge for this relation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-C002","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 is a procedural calculation step assigned to the aggregator/local coordinator. It is bound to coordination.local_operator, the only frozen node, with no frozen edge supplied."}],"revision_requests":["B source audit is required for v141-b-g02-e15 and v141-b-g02-e21; specifically resolve e21's prose 'other customers' versus displayed \\sum_{i\\in I} e_i^t(\\bar{x}^{(k)}) before any future formalization of the distributed information requirement."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
